Finally, our results enlighten the plasticity of the tubulin subunits. Interestingly, in microtubules, the \(\alpha\) subunit undergoes the most substantial structural variations associated with GTP hydrolysis (Manka and Moores, 2018; Zhang et al., 2015, 2018). Our data indicate that a conformational change of \(\alpha\)-tubulin toward the microtubule structure may be initiated outside the microtubule context. However, the full microtubular conformation has been seen only in microtubules and related assemblies (Löwe et al., 2001; Zhang et al., 2015) and remains to be captured in soluble tubulin complexes.
